.TH CPAU\-WATER "1" "2026\-05\-06" "cpau" "Generated Python Manual"
.SH NAME
cpau\-water
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cpau\-water
[-h] [--version] [-s | -v] [--secrets-file SECRETS_FILE] [-i {billing,monthly,daily,hourly}] [-o OUTPUT_FILE] [--cache-dir CACHE_DIR] start_date [end_date]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download water meter usage data from the City of Palo Alto WaterSmart portal. Authenticates via SAML/SSO using the credentials file (default: ~/.cpau/secrets.json) and emits CSV. The first invocation runs a headless browser to obtain a session cookie; subsequent invocations reuse the cached cookie from \-\-cache\-dir for fast (~1 second) authentication. Supported intervals are billing, monthly, daily, and hourly. The output column 'gallons' carries the usage value (water meters do not report kWh). If end_date is omitted it defaults to today; when start_date is later than today, an empty CSV is emitted (header only, exit 0) rather than treating the synthesized inverted range as an error.

.TP
\fBstart_date\fR
Start date for data retrieval in YYYY\-MM\-DD format (e.g., 2024\-12\-01)

.TP
\fBend_date\fR
End date for data retrieval in YYYY\-MM\-DD format (default: today)

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit

.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-silent\fR
supress non\-error logging

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
log debug\-level processing information

.TP
\fB\-\-secrets\-file\fR \fI\,SECRETS_FILE\/\fR
Path to JSON file with 'userid' and 'password' fields (default: $CPAU_SECRETS_FILE or ~/.cpau/secrets.json)

.TP
\fB\-i\fR \fI\,{billing,monthly,daily,hourly}\/\fR, \fB\-\-interval\fR \fI\,{billing,monthly,daily,hourly}\/\fR
Time interval for data retrieval (default: billing)

.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fI\,OUTPUT_FILE\/\fR, \fB\-\-output\-file\fR \fI\,OUTPUT_FILE\/\fR
Path to output file (default: stdout)

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-dir\fR \fI\,CACHE_DIR\/\fR
Directory for caching authentication cookies (default: ~/.cpau)

.SH COMMENTS
examples:
  cpau\-water \-\-interval daily 2025\-01\-01 2025\-01\-31
  cpau\-water \-\-interval hourly 2025\-01\-01 > water_hourly.csv
  cpau\-water \-\-interval billing 2024\-01\-01 2024\-12\-31 \-o billing.csv

